      {
        "q": "What if my sales change by season?",
        "a": "Run high- and low-season cases instead of using your best month. Compare the fixed requirement with slower months and decide what stronger months must set aside. ## Takeaways - Startup cash and monthly break-even are different calculations. Keep launch purchases and recurring operating costs separate. - Break-even should cover monthly fixed costs, owner pay, and target profit, after variable selling costs are deducted. - Inventory, margin, average order value, and order volume can change the answer more than the platform. - Round orders up and plan for cash timing, not just a tidy profit-and-loss result."
      }
